  # --- external resources the analysis draws on ---------------------------
  - type: database
    title: "CellChatDB v2 (human ligand-receptor interactions)"
    url: "https://github.com/jinworks/CellChat"
    authors:
      - name: "Suoqin Jin and others"
    notes: >-
      Pinned at a commit in config/ligand_receptor.yaml; P4-T2 reads the .rda
      with base R load() in the existing r-geomx environment.
  - type: database
    title: "NanoString CellProfileLibrary (SpatialDecon reference matrices)"
    url: "https://github.com/Nanostring-Biostats/CellProfileLibrary"
    authors:
      - name: "NanoString Biostatistics"
    notes: >-
      Lung_HCA and Brain_Darmanis, pinned at a commit SHA in config/config.yaml.
  - type: database
    title: "TCGA-LUAD expression and survival (UCSC Xena)"
    url: "https://xenabrowser.net/"
    authors:
      - name: "UCSC Xena"
    notes: >-
      P5-T4's external cohort, n = 502 with 182 events. ADR 0027 §5 bounds the
      comparison: GeoMx measures the PanCK-negative segment and TCGA whole bulk
      tumour, and there is no brain comparator at all.
  - type: database
    title: "EMBL-EBI Ontology Lookup Service (OLS4)"
    url: "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/"
    authors:
      - name: "EMBL-EBI"
    notes: >-
      Every ontology term in metadata/ontology-terms.tsv is resolved live
      against OLS4 on each build and asserted against the CURIE pinned in
      config/ontology_terms.yaml (P6-T2a).

  # --- agent skills, per PROJECT_PLAN §6 P6-T3 ----------------------------
  # The collection is cited as a whole AND the individual skills this project
  # actually used are named. 168 skills are installed and pinned by
  # skills-lock.json; naming all of them as "used" would be a citation of an
  # inventory rather than of a dependency.
  - type: software
    title: "scientific-agent-skills (K-Dense collection)"
    url: "https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills"
    authors:
      - name: "K-Dense AI"
    notes: >-
      163 of the 168 skills pinned in skills-lock.json come from this
      collection. Restore with `npx skills experimental_install`.
  - type: software
    title: "marimo-team/skills — marimo-notebook, jupyter-to-marimo, wasm-compatibility"
    url: "https://github.com/marimo-team/skills"
    authors:
      - name: "marimo team"
    notes: >-
      Notebook authoring, the §4.5 conversion route for incoming Jupyter
      material, and the WASM export check for app-tier notebooks.
  - type: software
    title: "marimo-team/marimo-pair — marimo-pair, retro-marimo-pair"
    url: "https://github.com/marimo-team/marimo-pair"
    authors:
      - name: "marimo team"
    notes: >-
      Live-kernel pairing. Nothing found in a pairing session is a result until
      a Snakemake rule produces it (CLAUDE.md hard constraint 5).
  - type: software
    title: "geomx-dsp-analysis (project-local skill)"
    url: "https://github.com/jjevans25/NSCLC_BM_Spatial_Transcriptomics"
    authors:
      - given-names: Jarrett
        family-names: Evans
    notes: >-
      Written for this project and committed with it: GeoMx assay vocabulary,
      Q3 normalisation, detection filtering and the SpatialDecon reference-matrix
      caveat. Source rather than an installed dependency, so skills-lock.json
      cannot restore it.
